@@ -40,7 +40,13 @@ Style: terse bullets, grep-friendly `##` headers, facts recovered from code (202
 - One cart per market, kept for the browser session only.
 - Add-to-cart adds one unit; quantity editable; quantity 0 removes the line; empty cart links to all products.
 - Guest cart is not merged into an account on sign-in; a signed-in shopper is attached to the cart on entering checkout; sign-out detaches all carts.
-- Add-to-cart failures are not shown to the shopper (gap, `docs/TODO.md`).
+- Add-to-cart failures show on the product page. Cart-drawer quantity changes still show none, including age-restriction rejections (gap, `docs/TODO.md`).
+
+## Age-restricted products
+- Merchant flags products as age-restricted in Saleor; the shop sets one minimum age (1-120) for all of them.
+- Listings and product pages show an age label (`{N}+`). Restricted products stay listed for everyone.
+- Buying needs a signed-in shopper whose account has a birthday that meets the minimum age. Guests are sent to sign in; signed-in shoppers without a birthday are asked to set one; underage shoppers get a notice and cannot buy. Saleor decides at add-to-cart and at checkout.
+- Birthday is optional at sign-up and editable in account settings. It is self-declared; there is no ID check.
 
 ## Checkout
 - Steps: Contact (email, shipping address) -> Shipping method (skipped if nothing ships) -> Payment (billing, pay). Browser Back walks steps.
